00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:01,580
(Transcribed by TurboScribe. Go Unlimited to remove this message.) Sweet Home Alabama.

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:04,280
You've heard it at a wedding, a ball

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,320
game, on a long drive with the windows

4
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:06,660
down.

5
00:00:07,660 --> 00:00:09,440
But the band that made it wasn't from

6
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:09,860
Alabama.

7
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:12,060
They were from Jacksonville, Florida.

8
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:15,740
And the song started as a comeback, aimed

9
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:17,920
at Neil Young, who had written two songs

10
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,920
calling out the South for its racism.

11
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:23,200
In the middle of all that, the song

12
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,880
gives a shout out to a few session

13
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:27,780
musicians in a tiny Alabama town of about

14
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:29,160
16,000 people.

15
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:31,400
That's the thing about Alabama.

16
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:33,380
It's already in your life.

17
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:34,860
You just never noticed.
